    "report": "Messaging and Notifications now take every time they decide or record from the application clock, and nothing in them reads the machine's time. The work is committed as `2d66432` on `main`, not pushed. All tests pass: 1049 unit and 607 e2e, with typecheck and lint clean.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Domain methods take the instant as a required parameter:** `Conversation.send`, `report` and `start`, `NoticeWindow.admit`, `MessageNoticeOwing.owe`, and `Notice.accept`. The `new Date()` defaults are gone.\n- **Handlers take the `Clock` in their constructor,** as the repo's architecture convention asks: `StartConversationCommandHandler`, `SendMessageCommandHandler`, `ReportMessageCommandHandler`, `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler`, and `NoticeDelivery`.\n- **Wiring passes the clock:** `messagingWiring` and `notificationsWiring` take it from `createApplication`, which passes the `openStayClock` it already builds. The `() => new Date()` default on `messagingWiring` is gone.\n- **Specs:** the specs that call the changed methods now pass a fixed instant. No assertions changed.\n\n**Decisions you may want to revisit**\n- `ReportMessageCommandHandler` read no time before, but `Conversation.report` defaulted its `reportedAt`, so the handler now takes the clock too.\n- `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler` reads the clock once per event and reuses that instant for conflict retries, so one event is decided at one moment.\n- `notificationsWiring` takes `clock` as its third argument, before the defaulted `messageNoticeWindowSeconds`, which TypeScript requires. Its only caller is `createApplication`.\n- The `new Date(stored)` calls in `Conversation.ts` parse timestamps already stored, so I left them. They don't read the clock.\n- I committed to `main` because you said \"current branch\". The harness guidance normally says to branch off the default branch first, so say if you'd rather have a branch.\n\nI did not start a server, so port 4471 was not used. I also did not update the ADRs, which describe the clock rollout.",
